---
import Profile from "../layouts/Profile.astro";
import FieldPlate from "../components/FieldPlate.astro";
import PhotoStrip from "../components/PhotoStrip.astro";
---

<Profile slug="inventor" related={["quantum-physicist", "wellness-rd", "apps"]}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    A faint nebula takes time to photograph. From a city rooftop, the sky keeps
    moving and the streetlights keep shining. I put together{" "}
    <a href="#purakaash">Purākaash Mk II</a> to work with both constraints.
  </Fragment>
  <div slot="lead" class="profile-actions">
    <a class="profile-button" href="https://vishwavigyan.com/purakaash.html">
      Open the illustrated build record
    </a>
  </div>
  <FieldPlate
    slot="plate"
    photo="rooftop-telescope"
    label="Instrument / Purākaash Mk II"
    caption="On the roof with the assembled telescope and its hand controller."
  />

  <section class="folio-row" id="purakaash">
    <div>
      <span class="stamp">Commissioned · October 2025</span>
      <h2>Keeping a star in place</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>
        A 203 mm optical tube gathers the light. As Earth turns, a guide camera
        watches a star and sends small corrections to the mount. That keeps the
        object on the same pixels while the main camera collects a long
        exposure.
      </p>
      <p>
        The cooled camera limits noise. Narrowband filters let through selected
        wavelengths emitted by glowing gas, helping a nebula stand out against
        city light. Each part solves a different problem.
      </p>
      <PhotoStrip
        items={[
          ["telescope-mount", "Adjusting the mount"],
          ["with-purakaash", "At the controls"],
        ]}
      />
      <p>
        My work was integrating the optics, mount, cameras and software through{" "}
        <a href="https://masterwithin.net/">Master Within</a>. The build also
        includes a guide in English and Bengali that explains setup, alignment
        and focus for a student at the instrument.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="folio-row">
    <h2>Other work at the bench</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Robotics and Vortex are part of my engineering work. I’m also exploring
        new equipment through Vishwa Vigyan. For the development and sourcing
        side of that work, see{" "}
        <a href="/wellness-rd/">my wellness R&amp;D profile</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        My <a href="/quantum-physicist/">physics work</a> takes me from an
        instrument pointed at the sky to a circuit cooled close to absolute
        zero.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Profile>
